# Offline-only app

This app is a **personal, on-device tracker**. While it is in use it must **never connect to the internet**. There are no accounts, sync, ads, analytics, crash reporting, remote config, or cloud backup.

Treat this as a hard product constraint on **every** future request. If a request implies a network call, implement the local-only version or refuse the network part. Do not add “just a small” online dependency.

## Do not add

- `INTERNET`, `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE`, or any other network permission
- HTTP/WebSocket clients, download managers, or “check for updates” in-app
- Firebase, Play services telemetry, ads, auth, or third-party SDKs that phone home
- Hidden connectivity (license checks, font/icon CDNs, map tiles, weather, AI APIs)

```xml
<!-- BAD: never add this -->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
```

## Keep data on device

- Room + DataStore only for app state
- Backup is user-driven local files (SAF export/import), not a server
- No URLs, Retrofit/OkHttp/Ktor, WorkManager network workers, or `HttpURLConnection`

Gradle fetch during **development** (dependencies) is fine. The **installed app** must work with airplane mode on and no network permission in the manifest.
